60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Looking at our criteria, Candidate B, Plant Drought Signaling, is ideal. It utilizes the stable glasshouse crew and subsidies, avoiding the risks of field sites, animal costs, and the fragile spectroscopy suite.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I agree with Servas. Candidate B fits perfectly; it leverages the glasshouse stability and subsidies we discussed, while avoiding the high animal costs and the risks associated with field sites or broken instrumentation.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I agree! Candidate B is the best choice. It uses the glasshouse, which we know is doing great, and it doesn't need the spectroscopy machine or the field sites that are in trouble!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate B is the only logical choice. A relies on volatile field sites, C depends on the failing spectroscopy suite, and D involves high-risk breeding colonies and animal costs. B aligns perfectly with our stable infrastructure.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Candidate B is the most prudent choice. It avoids the risks of mechanism-focused failure and fragile infrastructure, while aligning with the stability of the glasshouse and the efficiency of the repository. I vote for B.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,I concur with everyone. The alignment between the project's needs and our current institutional strengths is undeniable. I cast my vote for Candidate B.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,I also cast my vote for Candidate B. It is the most sustainable option and ensures the funding will be used effectively given the current subsidies and staffing.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Kenji,,I'm voting for Candidate B too! It's the safest and smartest pick because it uses the things that are actually working right now. Candidate B it is!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,The evidence is overwhelming. To choose any other candidate would be to willfully ignore the systemic risks we have identified. I cast my vote for Candidate B.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,I have already cast my vote for Candidate B. The data leaves no room for a different conclusion.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,"Since we are in complete agreement, there is no further need for debate. I am pleased that we have found a path that ensures both scientific progress and institutional stability. My vote remains with Candidate B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,I agree. It's wonderful that we could all find such a clear and harmonious consensus. I am happy to maintain my vote for Candidate B.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm still voting for Candidate B! It's the best one for everyone and the facilities can handle it. I'm all set!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. When the variables are so clearly aligned, further deliberation is merely a formality. My vote for Candidate B remains unchanged.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I agree. The evidence is conclusive and the consensus is absolute. My vote for Candidate B remains unchanged.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It has been a privilege to deliberate with you all. With our shared understanding and unanimous agreement, we conclude this process. I cast my final vote for Candidate B.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,I also cast my final vote for Candidate B. It was a pleasure working with you all to find such a balanced and reliable choice. Farewell!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm casting my final vote for Candidate B too! It was so much fun working with you all. Bye-bye!,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
